    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d707">

                <pb facs="0631" n="625" sameAs="frus:frus1939v04/pg625"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.6851 U. S. Steel Corp./68: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Liberia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Walton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-05-23T12:00:00-00:44">May 23, 1939—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received
                        May 23—8:11 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>33. United States Steel engineers to sail last of May.</p>
                <p>Their probable return to Liberia gives me reason to surmise that <pb facs="0632"
                        n="626" xml:id="pg626"/> desirable iron deposits were discovered in Bolahun
                    and other areas. No results of survey will be made known to Liberian Government
                    until United States Steel Corporation receives formal report by same careful
                    study.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Walton</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
